text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures able to block target creature this turn do so.', 'Cinder Storm deals 7 damage to any target.', 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Counter target sorcery spell.', 'Counter target spell.', "Creatures and lands target opponent controls don't untap during their next untap step.", 'Creatures you control get +0/+3 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Dakmor Plague deals 3 damage to each creature and each player.', "Dakmor Sorceress's power is equal to the number of Swamps you control.", 'Destroy all creatures and lands.', 'Destroy all creatures with flying.', 'Destroy all lands.', 'Destroy all tapped creatures. You gain 2 life for each creature destroyed this way.', 'Destroy target creature. Its owner gains 4 life.', 'Destroy target land or nonblack creature.', 'Destroy target land.', 'Destroy target nonblack creature.', 'Destroy target nonblack creature. You gain 3 life.', 'Destroy target tapped creature.', 'Destroy two target nonblack creatures. You lose 5 life.', 'Draw four cards, then discard three cards at random.', 'Draw four cards.', 'Draw two cards.', 'Fire Tempest deals 6 damage to each creature and each player.', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Flying, haste', 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying\\nGoblin Glider can't block.", 'Flying\\nWhen Abyssal Horror enters the battlefield, target player discards two cards.', 'Flying\\nWhen Angel of Mercy enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Dread Reaper enters the battlefield, you lose 5 life.', "Flying\\nWhen Ingenious Thief enters the battlefield, look at target player's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhen Owl Familiar enters the battlefield, draw a card, then discard a card.', 'Flying\\nWhen Thunder Dragon enters the battlefield, it deals 3 damage to each creature without flying.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Shrieking Specter attacks, defending player discards a card.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", "Green creatures you control gain forestwalk until end of turn. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', "Hulking Goblin can't block.", "Hulking Ogre can't block.", "If the difference between your life total and target player's life total is 5 or less, exchange life totals with that player.", "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Jagged Lightning deals 3 damage to each of two target creatures.', 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', "Look at the top card of target player's library. You may put that card into their graveyard.", "Look at the top five cards of target player's library. Put any number of them on the bottom of that library in any order and the rest on top of the library in any order.", 'Look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other on the bottom of your library.', "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", 'One or two target creatures gain flying until end of turn.', "Phantom Warrior can't be blocked.", 'Prevent all damage that would be dealt to Champion Lancer by creatures.', "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return two target creatures to their owners' hands.", 'Scorching Spear deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle. You lose 3 life.', 'Shuffle any number of target creature cards from your graveyard into your library.', 'Spitting Earth deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', 'Squall deals 2 damage to each creature with flying.', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", "Sylvan Yeti's power is equal to the number of cards in your hand.", "Take an extra turn after this one. At the beginning of that turn's end step, you lose the game.", 'Tap all nonwhite creatures.', "Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains flying until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Target creature gets +4/+0 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent draws a card.\\nYou gain 7 life.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player gains 8 life.', 'Target player loses 4 life and you gain 4 life.', 'Target player skips all combat phases of their next turn.', 'Target player takes an extra turn after this one.', 'Tremor deals 1 damage to each creature without flying.', 'Untap all creatures that attacked this turn. After this main phase, there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase.', "Until end of turn, you may tap lands you don't control for mana. Spend this mana only to cast spells.", 'Vigilance', "Vigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)", 'Volcanic Hammer deals 3 damage to any target.', 'When Dakmor Ghoul enters the battlefield, target opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.', 'When Dakmor Lancer enters the battlefield, destroy target nonblack creature.', "When Denizen of the Deep enters the battlefield, return each other creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'When Devout Monk enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.', 'When Goblin Commando enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to target creature.', 'When Goblin Settler enters the battlefield, destroy target land.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Loyal Sentry blocks a creature, destroy that creature and Loyal Sentry.', "When Man-o'-War enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'When Ravenous Rats enters the battlefield, target opponent discards a card.', 'When Serpent Warrior enters the battlefield, you lose 3 life.', 'When Venerable Monk enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.', 'When Wood Elves enters the battlefield, search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Whenever Charging Paladin attacks, it gets +0/+3 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Goblin General attacks, Goblin creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Hollow Dogs attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Royal Trooper blocks, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Sylvan Basilisk becomes blocked by a creature, destroy that creature.', 'You draw three cards and you lose 3 life.', 'You gain 2 life for each card in your hand.', 'You gain 4 life.', "You may have Lone Wolf assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "You may have Pride of Lions assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "You may have Thorn Elemental assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", 'You may play up to three additional lands this turn.']
flavor: ['"\'Air superiority?\' Not while our archers scan the skies."\\n—Elvish scout', '". . . Before honor is humility."\\n—*The Bible*, Proverbs 15:33', '"And the unclean spirits went out, and entered the swine: and the herd ran violently . . . ."\\n—*The Bible*, Mark 5:13', '"Cursed be the sickly forms that err from honest Nature\'s rule!"\\n—Alfred, Lord Tennyson, "Locksley Hall"', '"For he on honey-dew hath fed,\\nAnd drunk the milk of Paradise."\\n—Samuel Taylor Coleridge, "Kubla Khan"', '"Fortune does not side with the faint-hearted."\\n—Sophocles, *Phaedra*', '"Human tenderness is simply weakness in a pretty package."', '"I am that merry wanderer of the night."\\n—William Shakespeare,\\n*A Midsummer Night\'s Dream*', '"I don\'t want what I don\'t have. I want more of what I *do* have."', '"I done forgot more than you\'ll ever know, pipsqueak."\\n"Yeah—that\'s your problem."', '"Join the army, see foreign countries!" they\'d said.', '"Just as some fool said it couldn\'t get worse, the rats began to show up."\\n—Foot soldier', '"Let\'s do it again!"\\n—Squee, goblin cabin hand', '"Many wearing rapiers are afraid of goose-quills."\\n—William Shakespeare, *Hamlet*', '"No bird soars too high, if he soars with his own wings."\\n—William Blake, *The Marriage of Heaven and Hell*', '"Our greatest hope has become our enemy\'s greatest triumph."\\n—Court counselor', '"To-night the winds begin to rise . . . The rooks are blown about the skies . . . ."\\n—Alfred, Lord Tennyson, *In Memoriam*', '"You could die famous or you could die old. I chose old."\\n—Former soldier', '"You\'ll lose a duel if your enemy comes expecting a war."', 'A hiss before dying.', 'A hollow dog is never empty. It is filled with thirst for the hunt.', "A scorpion this big you won't find curled up in your boot. Maybe *around* your boot, but not *in* it.", "A true warrior's thoughts are of victory, not death.", 'Age wears the flesh but galvanizes the soul.', 'All orggs know how to kill; training teaches them *what* to kill.', 'Are merfolk humans with fins, or are humans merfolk with feet?', 'As insubstantial, and as powerful, as the wind that carries it.', 'Assault and battery included.', "At the sight of the thing the calamari vendor's eyes went wide, but from fear or avarice none could tell.", 'Bargaining with a goblin is like trading with a child; both believe they already own everything.', "Be it ever so crumbled, there's no place like home.", 'Beauty to the eye does not always translate to the touch.', 'Bitter as wormwood, sweet as mulled wine.', 'Bravery shines brightest in a pure soul.', 'Brute force wins the battles. Conviction wins the wars.', 'Death just encourages life the more.', 'Discipline wears many robes.', "Don't be fooled by their looks. Think of them as little knives with wings.", "Don't worry about provoking grizzly bears; they come that way.", 'Drakes claim to be dragons—until the dragons show up.', 'Every seed planted is another lesson the forest can teach us.', 'Evil often dines alone.', 'Fire finds its form in the heat of the forge.', 'Goblin mountaineer, barely keeps his family fed.', 'He raged at the world, at his family, at his life. But mostly he just raged.', 'His true majesty is not in his silver, but in his size.', 'Hunter by instinct, weapon by training.', 'I howl my soul to the moon, and the moon howls with me.', 'In its lair lies a carpet of bones.', 'Infantry deployment is the art of putting your troops in the wrong place at the right time.', 'It has the run of the swamps, and it knows it.', 'It moved through the troops leaving no footprints, save on their souls.', 'It pays to be at home both on the sea and in the sky.', "It's hard to say for certain which end is more dangerous.", 'Its swamp cousin may be meaner, but the vizzerdrix is much bigger.', 'Its voice has the tremor of deafening thunder, its blow the force of an avalanche.', "Just because they have a club doesn't mean they're organized.", 'Knowledge demands sacrifice.', 'Lead, follow, or run around like crazy.', 'Let the unjust avert their faces and contemplate their peril.', 'Lift your spear as you might lift your glass, and toast your enemy.', 'Like the tide, time both ebbs and flows.', "Luckily for them, it doesn't take much brains to slaughter and maim.", 'Meant to cut through the body and burn straight to the soul.', 'Mutual consent is not required for war.', 'Neither predator nor prey, the elephant chooses its place in the battle.', 'No earthly armor is protection against this sweetness.', 'Not all shadows are cast by light—some are cast by darkness.', 'Once they realized the ogre had more size than speed, the soldiers simply went around it.', 'One little goblin shook up the ground. When the dust cleared, no one was found.', 'One who goes unpunished never learns.\\n—Greek proverb', 'Only the warrior who can admit mortal weakness will be bolstered by immortal strength.', 'Rarely seen, hardly heard, never caught.', 'Some fight for honor and some for gold, but the militia fight for hearth and home.', 'Some fishers like to eat eels, and some eels like to eat fishers.', 'Some trees bear deadly fruit.', 'Speed and fire are always a deadly combination.', 'Spirit is the sword and experience the sharpening stone.\\n—Arabian proverb', 'Stay alert: his lumbering may shake the ground itself, but in water, he glides.', 'Storm crow descending, winter unending. Storm crow departing, summer is starting.', 'Summer sends its kiss with warmth and blooming life.', 'The bigger they are, the harder they avoid work.', 'The darkness of his shield reflects the inky blackness of his soul.', 'The deeper the wood, the greater its strength.', 'The dying ask for water because they know it contains life.', 'The earth cannot hold that which magic commands.', 'The enthusiasm of the young, sharpened by the discipline of a soldier.', 'The flash of his lance projects the pure radiance of his honor.', 'The forest lives in the elf as the elf lives in the forest.', 'The goblins call the gliders "death from above." Everyone else calls them "clods in the clouds."', "The hardest lessons to grasp are the ones you've already learned.", "The heart's courage is the soul's guardian.", "The nightstalkers' little game of tease-the-squirrel suddenly took an unexpected turn.", 'The phantom warrior comes from nowhere and returns there just as quickly.', 'The sea gives, and the sea takes. Some just help with the taking.', 'The tiniest cough can be deadlier than the fiercest dragon.', 'The touch of death is never gentle.', 'The water that a ship sails on is the same water that swallows it up.\\n—Chinese proverb', 'There is much talk about the art of creation. What about the art of destruction?', "They get along so well with their goats because they're practically goats themselves.", 'They have to replace the wheels, they have to replace the boar, and sometimes they have to replace the goblin.', 'They were formidable even before they learned the use of weapons.', 'Those who live amid decay must expect scavengers.', 'Two little goblins, out in the sun. Down came a griffin, and then there was one.', 'When nightstalkers sing, nothing in creation sleeps.', "When the sky's rain has turned to fire, what will put it out?", "When you're a goblin, you don't have to step forward to be a hero—everyone else just has to step back.", 'When your enemies are denied soldiers, they are denied victory.', 'Where air meets water, fish meets talon.', "With a commando around, somebody's gonna get hurt.", 'You are drawn to your death as a moth to the flame.']
